A procedure declared C-style: no colon on PROCEDURE or ENDPROC and a
parenthesized parameter list. procedure_declaration_syntax fires once on
the bare PROCEDURE token (missing-colon path); the same construct is not
also direct_procedure_call or unexpected_token. Records what the bare
ENDPROC line produces (diag.procedure_declaration_syntax).
-- input.ssl --
PROCEDURE CalcTax(nAmount);
	:RETURN nAmount * 0.2;
ENDPROC;
-- format --
PROCEDURE CalcTax(nAmount);
:RETURN nAmount * 0.2;
ENDPROC;
-- diagnostics --
1:1-1:10 error procedure_declaration_syntax: Procedure declarations require a leading colon. Use ":PROCEDURE Name;" (no parentheses; declare arguments via ":PARAMETERS").
-- diagnostics [--strict --info] --
1:1-1:10 error procedure_declaration_syntax: Procedure declarations require a leading colon. Use ":PROCEDURE Name;" (no parentheses; declare arguments via ":PARAMETERS").
1:1-1:10 warning undeclared_variable: Variable 'PROCEDURE' is not declared
1:19-1:26 warning undeclared_variable: Variable 'nAmount' is not declared
3:1-3:8 warning undeclared_variable: Variable 'ENDPROC' is not declared
